        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Xi hails China’s ‘unyielding’ ties with Russia as Putin visits Beijing Issued on: 20/05/2026 - 11:27 Chinese President Xi Jinping on Wednesday welcomed Russian President Vladimir Putin in Beijing at the start of a visit focused on energy security. The meeting comes on the heels of US president Donald Trump’s visit to the Chinese capital. France 24’s Andy Hilliar takes a look at the latest developments. 'Crony capitalism and oligarchy': 'Remarkable correlation' between Adani's rise & Modi’s ascendancy 20/05/2026 Asia / Pacific Race to contain ebola outbreak in war-torn DRC where weak infrastructure hampers response 20/05/2026 Africa Iran ‘prefers diplomacy’ but if there’s a war, Tehran says it’s ready 20/05/2026 Middle East 'Huge mismatch' between Iran, US and Gulf States' expectations, analyst says 19/05/2026 Middle East 'Russia and China share same goal in constructing alternative world order', analyst says 19/05/2026 Asia / Pacific Acting US attorney general defends fund for prosecuted Trump allies 19/05/2026 Americas 'Liquid on lips': Noughty makes premium alcohol-free wine 19/05/2026 Europe Putin lands in China for trip that aims to show unshakeable ties after Trump pomp 19/05/2026 Asia / Pacific Eldest son of Mango fashion empire founder held in murder inquiry into father's death 19/05/2026 Europe"
